{
  "schema": "calcdb.question/1",
  "probe": "r-sql-1/union-error-order",
  "bookRefs": [
    "R-SQL-1",
    "SQL-UNION-04"
  ],
  "description": "R-SQL-1 SQL-UNION-04: When a later or earlier UNION arm has a conversion failure (CLng over TX), are rows delivered before the error and at which call does it appear, with and without a final ORDER BY; and what do TOP inside arms with a final ORDER BY, and TOP over a UNION ALL with duplicates, return? Runs on a fresh copy of r-sql-1-accdb-main opened read-only through ACE DAO; each statement is opened with Database.OpenRecordset as a snapshot unless stated, Fields Name/Type/Size/SourceTable/SourceField are read before the first row, then every row's Field values to EOF (each MoveNext captured), then Close and DBEngine.Errors.",
  "callerSurface": "native-idispatch/x64",
  "invokeLcid": 1033,
  "observationRecipe": [
    "clearErrorInfoBefore",
    "excepinfo",
    "deferredFill",
    "errorInfo"
  ],
  "pathBinding": "attempt-local-copy",
